  "body": "The proposal is to introduce a new special element named `<shadowroot>` that if found in an HTML input stream ends up creating a shadow tree associated with its immediate parent. Any elements inside it end up in that shadow tree. It can be nested.\r\n\r\nThis will require changes to the parser and syntax section. We'll also need to figure out how we explain its macro-like behavior as `<shadowroot>` as element in a tree ends up as `HTMLUnknownElement` and would be non-conforming.\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/510 for the corresponding DOM thread. If we go ahead with this HTML and DOM will need to coordinate on the safelist for `attachShadow()` and make it a shared concept.\r\n\r\nWe'll also need to decide whether a `mode` attribute is to be required or whether we can find a suitable default here.\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/html-parser @whatwg/components ",
